# Your own core.hosts lines. Upgrades replace core.hosts and keep this
# file. pf apply installs the two as one, with this file second. Lines for
# a host that is already in core.hosts add to it, for kinds and headers.
#
#   host KIND[:Header[,Header...]] ...
#
# A placeholder is substituted only into Authorization (Bearer or Basic)
# and X-Api-Key. Name another header after the kind to add it for that
# host and kind, e.g.
#
#   gitlab.com GITLAB_TOKEN:PRIVATE-TOKEN
#
# pf enroll mint --header writes these lines for you. Headers that are
# logged or echoed, or that steer routing, can never be named: User-Agent,
# Referer, Origin, Host, Via, Forwarded, X-Forwarded-*, X-Real-IP,
# Content-*, Transfer-Encoding, Connection, Keep-Alive, Upgrade, TE,
# Trailer and Proxy-*.
